{
  "description": "The Cornell box: the classic test of global illumination, after the room built and photographed at Cornell in 1984. A white room with a red wall on the left and a green one on the right, lit only by a panel in the ceiling, holding a mirror ball, a glass ball and a matte one. Path tracing shows the red and green bleeding onto the white walls and the balls, the soft shadows of the panel, the light the glass ball gathers into a bright spot on the floor, and the room again in the mirror. Let it gather a few hundred samples.",
